Task complete. Summary:

**Deliverable:** `/work/submission.csv` — 299,844 rows, columns `[id, satisfaction]`, ids identical and in the same order as `/data/sample_submission.csv`, all values probabilities in [0,1], no nulls.

**Approach & results:**
- Data: 699,635 train rows, target ~44.4% satisfied; `Arrival Delay in Minutes` missing in both sets (filled with median + missing indicator); categoricals label-encoded.
- Features: ratings (avg/min/max), total/differential delay, delay-positive flags, age bin, Class×delay interaction (~41 features).
- Model: LightGBM, stratified 5-fold CV with ROC AUC and early stopping.
  - Baseline: mean CV AUC **0.95878** (std 0.00062), OOF 0.95877
  - Optuna (15 trials): best 0.95896 — gain within noise, so tuning was stopped per the diminishing-returns rule
- Final model retrained on full train data, test-set probabilities written to submission.

**Verification (passed):** format/ids/columns match the sample exactly; values in [0,1]. Local CV target (>0.90) met at ≈0.959.

**Note:** state files (`intent.md`, `evidence.md`, `aar.md`) are in `/work` instead of `/work/.harness` because that directory is owned by another user and not writable by me. `/data` was not modified; no internet used. Runtime well within the 60-minute budget (~40 min used).
